


**Application:** Shopify public website  
**Target URL:** [https://www.shopify.com/in](https://www.shopify.com/in)  
**Objective:** Check that key pages and public-facing interactions work across common browsers and screen sizes.

**In Scope**
- Homepage loading and primary content
- Navigation and links
- Prominent calls to action
- Responsive layout
- Basic accessibility and page performance checks

**Out of Scope**
- Merchant admin or authenticated workflows
- Payment processing, checkout, and store-specific functionality
- Load, security, and compatibility testing beyond basic smoke checks

**Test Environment**
- Current versions of Chrome, Firefox, and Edge
- Desktop and mobile viewport sizes
- Public internet access; no account required for the basic checks

| ID | Test | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| SHP-01 | Open the target URL | The page loads without a browser error; the main content is visible. |
| SHP-02 | Check the page title and primary heading | They are present and relevant to the page. |
| SHP-03 | Use the main navigation links | Each link opens its intended destination without a broken-page error. |
| SHP-04 | Select a prominent call-to-action | It opens the expected next page or flow. |
| SHP-05 | Use the site on a mobile-sized viewport | Content remains readable and controls usable without unintended horizontal scrolling. |
| SHP-06 | Check images and visible media | They load and do not appear broken or obscure page content. |
| SHP-07 | Navigate with the keyboard | Interactive controls can be reached and used with keyboard navigation. |
| SHP-08 | Reload the page and revisit it | The page remains accessible and loads consistently. |

**Entry Criteria:** The public site is reachable and the test environment has internet access.  
**Exit Criteria:** All planned checks are run; failures are recorded with browser, viewport, steps, and evidence.  
**Assumption:** This plan covers Shopify’s public marketing website, not an individual Shopify-powered store. Actual page content and destinations should be confirmed during execution.